Subject: [PATCH 0030] Aggregate the render phase profile into five log lines

The in-C render phase markers never fired.  DOOM_SBF_PHASE_PROFILE was defined
on the platform and codec archives and not on the engine archive, so the
R_DRAW_PHASE guard in r_draw.h was never true for the 41-TU cut and every
marker in r_main.c, r_segs.c, r_things.c and r_plane.c compiled out.  build.rs
now defines it on the engine archive too, and this patch replaces the log-per-
marker scheme with accumulate-then-emit, because even with the markers live a
flat list needs about fifteen lines for one strip and Solana keeps ten program
log lines per transaction.  The markers that survive a flat list are the early
ones, so the render split -- the thing the profile exists to measure -- is
exactly what gets dropped.  Here each site accumulates its own interval into a
context cell and the strip driver emits fifteen cells in five sol_log_64 lines.

The cells are the last two members of doom_ctx_t in a diagnostic build
(eighteen accumulators and four mark registers, 176 bytes), so every field
offset above them and the zone arena are unchanged.  They live in the context
account rather than in C or Rust statics because the image must carry zero
writable static data (M1006 measured the loader refusal for .data and for .bss
alike).  doom_sbf_prof_cu and doom_sbf_prof_log are Rust shims: the
freestanding C headers in sbfinc/ declare no syscall interface.

The whole accumulator, the accessor macros and the two struct members are
inside #ifdef DOOM_SBF_PHASE_PROFILE, so it is compiled only into a
diagnostic-profile image.  The first version of this patch declared the cells
unconditionally, which put 176 bytes in EVERY build and moved CTX_MIN_BYTES,
CTX_STRUCT_BYTES, BOOTSTRAP_OFFSET and ACCOUNT_BYTES with it; the merge of
7f3cfa7c3 was reverted for that reason (30088de1f).  Making the cells
conditional is what keeps a production image byte-identical in layout to one
built without this patch, which is the property deployed images, live context
accounts and the sender scripts all depend on.  A build that grows the
context struct is a consensus change, and a diagnostic-only measurement must
not be one.  The accumulator adds the same two meter reads per interval in a
phase-profile image and a count-only image, so it cancels in the store-cost
difference between those two.

Two of the PROF_ENTER sites (R_RenderSegLoop, R_AddSprites) sit after their
declaration blocks rather than before them: the macro is ((void)0) outside a
diagnostic build, and a statement ahead of a declaration is not C90.  The
interval is identical either way.

Slots, in emission order, three per line:
  0 fixed pre-render   (ctx guard, layout rebind, arena rebind, dynamic state
                        import, framebuffer allocation, screen and view bases)
  1 R_SetupFrame       2 R_ClearClipSegs/DrawSegs/Planes/Sprites
  3 R_RenderBSPNode    4   of which R_RenderSegLoop
  5   of which R_AddSprites
  6 R_DrawPlanes       7   of which R_MapPlane's per-column setup
  8 R_DrawMasked       9   of which R_SortVisSprites
 10   of which the vissprite draw loop
 11   of which the masked mid-texture seg range loop
 12   of which R_DrawPlayerSprites
 13 fixed post-render  (strip extraction, free, arena rewind)
 14 the 32-root relink and the arena rebind alone, so the dynamic state import
    beside them can be priced apart (0 minus 14 is the state import and the
    framebuffer allocation)
 15 R_RenderPlayerView as a whole, as a cross-check on 1,2,3,6,8
 16 rsn3_apply_dynamic, the dynamic state import
 17 the framebuffer allocation, the screen pointers, ylookup and the view bases

Applies on top of 0001-0017 and 0021.

--- a/linuxdoom-1.10/headless/doom_ctx.h
+++ b/linuxdoom-1.10/headless/doom_ctx.h
@@ -50,6 +50,69 @@
  * decoder failure threshold. */
 #define DOOM_SBF_PRIVATE_BYTES 32
 
+/* Patch 0030: diagnostic render-phase accumulator.  DOOM_SBF_PROF_SLOTS
+ * unsigned-long cells, declared as the LAST member of doom_ctx_t for the same
+ * reason patch 0017 used doom_sbf_private: every field offset above is
+ * unchanged.
+ *
+ * The cells are compiled ONLY under DOOM_SBF_PHASE_PROFILE.  build.rs defines
+ * that on the platform, engine and codec archives of a `diagnostic-profile`
+ * image and on nothing else, so a production build -- host or SBF, qualifying
+ * or not -- keeps exactly the sizeof(doom_ctx_t) it had before this patch.
+ * That matters beyond tidiness: the static resource header records
+ * CTX_STRUCT_BYTES at offset 20, the deployed images and the live context
+ * accounts are sized from it, and a build that grew the struct by 176 bytes
+ * would have made every one of them wrong at once.  The first version of this
+ * patch declared the cells unconditionally, which put those 176 bytes in
+ * every build; see the revert of this patch (30088de1f) for the incident.
+ *
+ * Eighteen slots fit in six sol_log_64 lines, which is what makes a nested
+ * phase split reportable at all: a flat marker list overruns Solana's
+ * ten-line per-transaction program log and the late markers are the ones that
+ * get dropped. */
+#ifdef DOOM_SBF_PHASE_PROFILE
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_SLOTS 18
+
+/* Four mark registers, so a nested split (R_RenderBSPNode with R_RenderSegLoop
+ * and R_AddSprites inside it) does not overwrite its own start reading.  The
+ * depth is passed explicitly at each site instead of tracked in a counter:
+ * the depths in use are 0 for whole-strip phases, 1 for R_RenderPlayerView
+ * and 2 for the BSP interior, and an explicit lvalue keeps the macros usable
+ * in a void expression under -std=gnu89. */
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_MARKS 4
+
+/* Slot names.  The numbering is the order the cells are emitted in, three per
+ * sol_log_64 line, and it is recorded in the design note; changing it changes
+ * the reading of a stored profile, so append rather than renumber. */
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_FIXED_PRE 0
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_SETUP_FRAME 1
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_CLEAR_BUFS 2
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_BSP 3
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_SEG_LOOP 4
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_ADD_SPRITES 5
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_DRAW_PLANES 6
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_PLANE_SETUP 7
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_DRAW_MASKED 8
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_SORT_VISSPR 9
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_VISSPRITES 10
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_MASKED_SEGS 11
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_PSPRITES 12
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_FIXED_POST 13
+/* The 32-root relink and the arena rebind on their own, so the dynamic state
+ * import they sit next to can be priced apart from them.  The prior note read
+ * the 1101-1102 interval as "layout and arena rebind", but that interval also
+ * contains rsn3_apply_dynamic, which re-imports every mobj and re-runs
+ * P_SetThingPosition for each. */
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_REBIND 14
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_RENDER_TOTAL 15
+/* The two halves of FIXED_PRE apart.  Slot 0 minus slot 14 was the only thing
+ * separating the dynamic state import from the framebuffer set-up, and which of
+ * them the fixed setup mostly is decides whether the fixed setup is worth
+ * attacking before a scene-once pass exists at all. */
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_RSN3_APPLY 16
+#define DOOM_SBF_PROF_FRAME_SETUP 17
+#endif /* DOOM_SBF_PHASE_PROFILE */
+
 typedef struct doom_ctx_s {
     unsigned long doom_ctx_probe_cell;
     int	easy;
@@ -475,6 +538,13 @@
     /* Last member on purpose: the zone arena and every field offset above are
      * unchanged, so only sizeof(doom_ctx_t) grows. */
     unsigned char doom_sbf_private[DOOM_SBF_PRIVATE_BYTES];
+#ifdef DOOM_SBF_PHASE_PROFILE
+    /* Last member on purpose (patch 0030): the zone arena and every field
+     * offset above are unchanged, and a build without the accumulator does
+     * not have them at all, so sizeof(doom_ctx_t) is unchanged too. */
+    unsigned long doom_sbf_prof[DOOM_SBF_PROF_SLOTS];
+    unsigned long doom_sbf_prof_mark[DOOM_SBF_PROF_MARKS];
+#endif
 } doom_ctx_t;
 
 void doom_ctx_init(void);
@@ -902,6 +972,31 @@
 #define doom_sbf_controller_applied ((int *)&DOOM_CTX->doom_sbf_private[8])
 #define doom_sbf_private_alloc_fail ((long *)&DOOM_CTX->doom_sbf_private[16])
 #define doom_sbf_private_alloc_calls ((long *)&DOOM_CTX->doom_sbf_private[24])
+#ifdef DOOM_SBF_PHASE_PROFILE
+#define doom_sbf_prof ((unsigned long *)DOOM_CTX->doom_sbf_prof)
+#define doom_sbf_prof_mark ((unsigned long *)DOOM_CTX->doom_sbf_prof_mark)
+#endif
+
+/* Patch 0030 accumulator.  doom_sbf_prof_cu is a Rust shim: the C side has
+ * no declaration for the remaining-CU syscall and the image must not gain
+ * writable static data, so the cells live in the context account and the two
+ * calls are extern.  Each PROF pair costs two meter reads; the reads cost the
+ * same in a phase-profile image and in a count-only image, so they cancel in
+ * the store-cost difference between the two. */
+#ifdef DOOM_SBF_PHASE_PROFILE
+extern unsigned long doom_sbf_prof_cu(void);
+#define PROF_ENTER(slot, depth) \
+    (doom_sbf_prof_mark[(depth)] = doom_sbf_prof_cu())
+/* The meter only ever falls, so the interval is the mark minus the later
+ * reading.  Written the other way round it underflows, which is unsigned
+ * arithmetic doing exactly what it was told. */
+#define PROF_EXIT(slot, depth) \
+    (doom_sbf_prof[(slot)] += \
+     doom_sbf_prof_mark[(depth)] - doom_sbf_prof_cu())
+#else
+#define PROF_ENTER(slot, depth) ((void)0)
+#define PROF_EXIT(slot, depth) ((void)0)
+#endif
 #define doom_error_latched (DOOM_CTX->doom_error_latched)
 #define doom_sbf_demo_done (DOOM_CTX->doom_sbf_demo_done)
 #define doom_render_fuzz_columns (DOOM_CTX->doom_render_fuzz_columns)
--- a/linuxdoom-1.10/r_draw.h
+++ b/linuxdoom-1.10/r_draw.h
@@ -41,12 +41,13 @@
  * store, so the CU difference between a phase-profile image and a count-only
  * image is the pixel-write cost of the drawers.  Both defines are
  * diagnostic-only and must never appear in a deployable image. */
-#ifdef DOOM_SBF_PHASE_PROFILE
-extern void doom_sbf_phase_marker(unsigned long phase);
-#define R_DRAW_PHASE(phase) doom_sbf_phase_marker((unsigned long)(phase))
-#else
+/* Patch 0030: these markers no longer log.  A flat marker list needs fifteen
+ * lines for one strip and Solana keeps ten per transaction, so the markers
+ * that DO get through are the early ones and the render split -- the part the
+ * measurement is for -- is exactly what is dropped.  PROF_ENTER/PROF_EXIT
+ * (doom_ctx.h, force-included into every archive) accumulate instead, and the
+ * strip driver emits all of them in five aggregated lines. */
 #define R_DRAW_PHASE(phase) ((void)0)
-#endif
 
 
 
--- a/linuxdoom-1.10/r_main.c
+++ b/linuxdoom-1.10/r_main.c
@@ -832,36 +832,48 @@
 //
 void R_RenderPlayerView (player_t* player)
 {	
+    PROF_ENTER(DOOM_SBF_PROF_RENDER_TOTAL, 0);
+    PROF_ENTER(DOOM_SBF_PROF_SETUP_FRAME, 1);
     R_SetupFrame (player);
     R_DRAW_PHASE(1201);
+    PROF_EXIT(DOOM_SBF_PROF_SETUP_FRAME, 1);
 
     // Clear buffers.
+    PROF_ENTER(DOOM_SBF_PROF_CLEAR_BUFS, 1);
     R_ClearClipSegs ();
     R_ClearDrawSegs ();
     R_ClearPlanes ();
     R_ClearSprites ();
     R_DRAW_PHASE(1202);
-    
+    PROF_EXIT(DOOM_SBF_PROF_CLEAR_BUFS, 1);
+
     // check for new console commands.
     NetUpdate ();
 
     // The head node is the last node output.
+    PROF_ENTER(DOOM_SBF_PROF_BSP, 1);
     R_RenderBSPNode ((DOOM_CTX->numnodes)-1);
     R_DRAW_PHASE(1203);
+    PROF_EXIT(DOOM_SBF_PROF_BSP, 1);
     
     // Check for new console commands.
     NetUpdate ();
     
+    PROF_ENTER(DOOM_SBF_PROF_DRAW_PLANES, 1);
     R_DrawPlanes ();
     R_DRAW_PHASE(1204);
+    PROF_EXIT(DOOM_SBF_PROF_DRAW_PLANES, 1);
     
     // Check for new console commands.
     NetUpdate ();
     
+    PROF_ENTER(DOOM_SBF_PROF_DRAW_MASKED, 1);
     R_DrawMasked ();
     R_DRAW_PHASE(1205);
+    PROF_EXIT(DOOM_SBF_PROF_DRAW_MASKED, 1);
 
     // Check for new console commands.
     NetUpdate ();
     R_DRAW_PHASE(1206);
+    PROF_EXIT(DOOM_SBF_PROF_RENDER_TOTAL, 0);
 }
--- a/linuxdoom-1.10/r_plane.c
+++ b/linuxdoom-1.10/r_plane.c
@@ -149,6 +149,7 @@
     angle = (viewangle + xtoviewangle[x1])>>ANGLETOFINESHIFT;
     ds_xfrac = viewx + FixedMul(finecosine[angle], length);
     ds_yfrac = -viewy - FixedMul(finesine[angle], length);
+    PROF_ENTER(DOOM_SBF_PROF_PLANE_SETUP, 2);
 
     if (fixedcolormap)
 	ds_colormap = fixedcolormap;
@@ -165,9 +166,16 @@
     ds_y = y;
     ds_x1 = x1;
     ds_x2 = x2;
+
+    /* Patch 0030: everything above the spanfunc() call is the plane pass's
